{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1551815-best-antagonists","id":1551815,"title":"Best Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-22T04:03:38-07:00","id":1551815,"title":"Best Antagonists","content":"I'm looking for some of the best antagonists across gamelines.<br /> <br /> I think so far Werewolf has some of the absolute best by far.<br /> <br /> Hosts, Geryo, Idigami, and even Shadow Occultists are great having such diversity and character.<br /> <br /> Exiled angels from Demon also feature this diversity and character...<br /> <br /> But special mention should go to Echos (from demon) and the Strix. The only issue with these is that they are great as antagonists for their specific game line.<br /> <br /> The Strix are amazing if you are already playing paranoid vampire politics-game.<br /> <br /> And Echos are a deeply disturbing consequence of your actions, but can only really be understood for a Demon.<br /> <br /> So what antagonists am I missing that you love? What are the best either for a specific gameline or generally as antagonists for any game (including a blue book mortals game)?<br /> <br /> And most importantly, why do you love them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-22T07:47:06-07:00","id":1551817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1551815-best-antagonists#post1551815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking for some of the best antagonists across gamelines.<br /> <br /> I think so far Werewolf has some of the absolute best by far.<br /> <br /> Hosts, Geryo, Idigami, and even Shadow Occultists are great having such diversity and character.<br /> <br /> Exiled angels from Demon also feature this diversity and character...<br /> <br /> But special mention should go to Echos (from demon) and the Strix. The only issue with these is that they are great as antagonists for their specific game line.<br /> <br /> The Strix are amazing if you are already playing paranoid vampire politics-game.<br /> <br /> And Echos are a deeply disturbing consequence of your actions, but can only really be understood for a Demon.<br /> <br /> So what antagonists am I missing that you love? What are the best either for a specific gameline or generally as antagonists for any game (including a blue book mortals game)?<br /> <br /> And most importantly, why do you love them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are the Echos detailed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-22T08:27:29-07:00","id":1551819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1551815-best-antagonists?p=1551817#post1551817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are the Echos detailed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Echoes are in the Tools of the Machine section of the Demon Storyteller's Guide. They rarely come about when a demon burns a soul pact, modeled as ghosts of the person whose soul was taken to make the Cover, anchored to bits of their old life as usual along with to the demon themself. They're able to use Embeds, Exploits, and angelic Numina, and can reflexively penalize rolls for Embeds and Exploits made by the demon who burned their soul. They seek to destroy their nemesis in some fashion, whether by killing them, dismantling their lives, or forcing them to expose themselves to the Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-22T10:31:37-07:00","id":1551820,"title":"","content":"What about Charlatans, True Fae exiles, bound to roam the material realm until they fulfill a certain goal or oath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-24T00:51:59-07:00","id":1551838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1551815-best-antagonists?p=1551820#post1551820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Charlatans, True Fae exiles, bound to roam the material realm until they fulfill a certain goal or oath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know much about Charlatans. They are still True Fae, but not as powerful? Being stuck Iron-side doesn't sound like the best plan...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-24T09:06:55-07:00","id":1551842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1551815-best-antagonists?p=1551838#post1551838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about Charlatans. They are still True Fae, but not as powerful? Being stuck Iron-side doesn't sound like the best plan...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a plan, though some of them may have seen it coming.<br /> <br /> Charlatans are Fae who have become stuck in the mortal world, whether due to banishment, connecting with mortals, or dying from prolonged exposure to Earth and deciding going native was better than lasting death. Their mien becomes subtler and harder to distinguish from a human, and depending on how they became what they are they might not remember enough about their origins to use the powers they retain (though they still have access to them); they're barred from the Hedge, but they're as durable as before and run the full gamut of Wyrd scores. Depending on the individual specimen and how their life goes, they might become more different still, inverting their Virtue and Vice to recover Willpower like a human does or stranger things yet.<br /> <br /> Charlatans are notable as antagonists because they're True Fae on Earth with some of the limitations that usually applies removed and they have agendas that they lack the Clarity or Morality to hold them back from pursuing with abandon. They're not mentioned much outside their introductory book because they were in Changeling 1e's very first supplement (and, as is often the case with books being written at the same time as the corebook, there's some quirks in the writing) and the basic premise they exist as a workaround for has been functionally replaced in 2e by the Gentry being bound by the Bargains of local Courts, but &quot;stranded Fae who forgot what it is or is desperately trying to get home&quot; is a solid category of antagonist to build around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-24T18:00:05-07:00","id":1551847,"title":"","content":"Charlatans are also cool because they are antagonists in a more ambiguous space. It might be possible to coexist with a charlatan peacefully. It might be a way the Good Folk could learn to gather something closer to a human perspective. It might be a way they grow!<br /> <br /> But a charlatan isn't a changeling. They'll never really be human. Somewhere down there is the heart of the Other, and even if they're not lying about their newfound emotions leading them to care about what happens to you and not want to betray you, when will the other shoe drop, how will it slip out? What form will it take when they show you that as much as they might be trying, they're a creature whose instincts and reflexes are to view other beings as toys and props?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T08:35:37-07:00","id":1551857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1551815-best-antagonists?p=1551847#post1551847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlatans are also cool because they are antagonists in a more ambiguous space. It might be possible to coexist with a charlatan peacefully. It might be a way the Good Folk could learn to gather something closer to a human perspective. It might be a way they grow!<br /> <br /> But a charlatan isn't a changeling. They'll never really be human. Somewhere down there is the heart of the Other, and even if they're not lying about their newfound emotions leading them to care about what happens to you and not want to betray you, when will the other shoe drop, how will it slip out? What form will it take when they show you that as much as they might be trying, they're a creature whose instincts and reflexes are to view other beings as toys and props?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda why I like Exiles, angels who still wanna Angel, pretty powerful entities in their own right, but without the connection to the God-Machine, for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> They can be a very ambugious space, willing to do most anything to feel purpose again? Or maybe they just do whatever their last order told them to do... Maybe they've been doing that for thousands of years...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T08:52:36-07:00","id":1551858,"title":"","content":"I loved Dizang, the exile bodhisattva from the Demon corebook, whose entire thing is just that he wants to talk to you about how you should return to the God-Machine. He's genuinely not going to rat on you or capture you or force you. He just thinks you should go back and he wants to try to convince you to agree to do so.<br /> <br /> Not really an antagonist in most cases, but an interesting supporting cast member.<br /> <br /> Similar vibes to Carl, the shapeshifting fishman from War Against the Pure, who's about to get caught up in the fishpeople cult uprising situation and feels helpless and distraught over it, because Carl's not a member of the Mother Ocean cult. Carl's a simple, unassuming golden rule Christian. Carl just wants to show tourists around the lake in his boat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 06-25-2025, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}